    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Jose Caballero** represents our strongest play with a stellar 80.26 efficiency score, buoyed by a prime matchup against J. Lopez and a significant dynamic platoon advantage that makes him a must-start in our pursuit of stolen bases. He is joined at the top of our priority list by **Corbin Carroll** (73.68) and **Brice Turang** (71.97); both benefit from favorable order positioning and high-leverage SP matchups that keep our Roto floors high. **James Wood** (71.33) is another standout, as his lead-off role against Canning offers a volume-heavy path to runs that fits perfectly with our emphasis on efficiency. We are also leaning on the favorable park factors and platoon splits for **Kyle Karros** and **Vinnie Pasquantino** to anchor the heart of the order, even as the team monitors the lineup status of **Seiya Suzuki**, who remains a solid start if he sticks in the #6 hole.\n\nThe most difficult decision on our bench was leaving **Austin Riley** on the sidelines despite his 51.66 score. While he brings raw power, his matchup against a high-skill arm like Lodolo and the fact that he faces an \"Elite Hold\" pitcher\u2014which suppresses his stolen base upside\u2014ultimately pushed him behind the likes of **Dalton Rushing** and **Alex Freeland**. We are sacrificing his ceiling to maintain a more balanced profile across our 5x5 categories. As we look at the margins, we are keeping a close eye on **Dalton Rushing**, whose efficiency score of 51.56 is buoyed by his status as an elite catcher, though we remain wary of his placement in the #8 slot. With **Mickey Moniak** sidelined on the IL, our depth is being tested, but the projected output from our current starters, including the steady presence of **Josh Naylor** and **Tyler Soderstrom**, positions Ghost Ride the WHIP to capture meaningful gains in the counting categories today.",
